`,JD=`// A field of grass that follows the car.
//
// The blades are one fixed buffer of triangles laid out on a grid, and every
// frame the grid is wrapped modulo its own size around the car's position. A
// blade that falls off the back edge reappears at the front, lands on whatever
// terrain is there, and takes that ground's height and colour. So the field is
// endless for a fixed vertex count and a single draw call, and nothing is
// allocated, sorted or culled per frame. This is folio-2025's approach; the
// edge fade below is not, and it is what stops the wrap from being visible.
//
